===Etymology===
{{compound|en|butter|cup}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbʌt.ə.kʌp/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbʌt.ɚ.kʌp/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-buttercup.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of many [[herb]]s, of the [[genus]] ''[[Ranunculus]]'', having [[yellow]] [[flower]]s; the [[crowfoot]].
# Any [[flower]] of the genus ''[[Narcissus]]''; a [[daffodil]].
# {{non-gloss definition|Affectionate or ironic term of address.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|lyricist=Otis Blackwell and Elvis Presley|title=All Shook Up|artist=Elvis Presley|year=1957|text=When she touched my hand, what a chill I got<br>Her lips are like a volcano that's hot<br>I'm proud to say that she's my '''buttercup'''.<br>I'm in love - I'm all shook up.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1987|author=Joyce Brandon|title=Lady and the Lawman|page=346|passage=Listen, '''buttercup''', you're damned good in bed. They don't come any better, but I'm really not interested in playing second fiddle to your camera or your young lovers.}}

